[c0004] c0004 is done and in `review`, committed as `b81e65c`.
[c0004] ## What changed
[c0004] **`LevelAsset` + `LevelAssetLoader`** (`src/level/asset.rs`) read `assets/levels/*.ron` through the asset server. `Levels` is now `Vec<Handle<LevelAsset>>`; `get_current_level` takes `&Assets<LevelAsset>` and returns an `Option`, and `get_current_level_mut` is gone. `arena`, `level`, `events` and `pickups` all cope with a level that hasn't arrived rather than unwrapping.
[c0004] **The card's open question resolved as it predicted.** Losing the `_mut` accessor forced `distributed_global_pickups` off `LevelDefinition` — it's now per-match state on `MatchState`, derived from the level's authored `global_pickups` and cleared by `reset()`. `pickup_spawn_globals_on_event` no longer needs `Levels` at all.
[c0004] **Two judgement calls I made rather than asking:**
[c0004] - Because levels now load asynchronously, `game_flow_handler` holds the `StartMatch` transition until `Levels::readiness` says `Ready`. Without it a first match could start in front of a level still in flight, so "plays exactly as before" would have been luck rather than a property.
[c0004] - Hot reload replaces the *blocks* of the running match, not the arena, ship or score. Rebuilding the background or obstacles mid-match means tearing down the 3D environment, which is `c0013`'s problem. I noted this scoping on the card.
[c0004] `bevy` gained the `file_watcher` feature — that's what makes a hand edit an `AssetEvent` at all.
[c0004] ## How it was checked
[c0004] `cargo build` clean, `cargo test` 53 passed (up from 40). Beyond tests, I ran the real game with a temporary auto-start system (since removed): adding a row of nine blocks to `level0.ron` in a text editor took the running match from 6 blocks to 15, logged live. Writing garbage into a level file reported the parse error naming `LevelAssetLoader`; restoring it reloaded cleanly.
[c0004] Two things I want to flag rather than bury:
[c0004] - **I could not play the levels through.** This session can't send input to the window, so "every level behaves exactly as before" rests on the campaign loading field-for-field equal to c0003's pre-migration literals, plus the block counts above — not on playing all seven.
[c0004] - **Known limitation:** if the level `GameState::NextLevel` moves to can't be loaded, the fallback to the menu restarts the campaign at level 0 rather than resuming. Only reachable by breaking a level file mid-run; it's on the card.
[c0004] `src/events/mod.rs` also carries Bevy 0.9→0.19 migration edits that were already uncommitted in the working tree — same arrangement as c0002 and c0003, disclosed in the commit message.
