[c0007] ## What landed
[c0007] **The format got its inverse** (`src/level/layout/mod.rs`)
[c0007] - `block_token` writes the token `make_block` would read a block back out of, sitting right next to it. A test walks all 2295 tokens the format defines through `make_block` and back.
[c0007] - `set_cell` rewrites the grid rather than patching one line, which pads every row to the widest one — `interpret_grid` takes the column count off the first line only, so a ragged grid centres its rows on a width they don't have. Painting one squares it up.
[c0007] - `filled_grid` spells a `FilledGrid` out as tokens.
[c0007] **Painting** (`src/editor/mod.rs`)
[c0007] - `Brush` holds type, behaviour, trigger and erase mode. Trigger type and group are *one* field, so the invalid brush the card warns about can't be built; `block_token` drops a trigger entirely rather than writing half of one.
[c0007] - Left button paints, right button erases, holding either drags a run of cells. `PaintStroke` opens on button-down and closes on button-up, so a drag is one edit — `c0011` has one entry to push.
[c0007] - A `FilledGrid` becomes a token grid the first time a cell of it is painted. That's every level file that names no layout, since `LevelDefinition::default` is `FilledGrid(5, 5, …)`.
[c0007] **The editor had no blocks in it at all before this** — `c0005` and `c0006` drew the grid and the hover, the level itself was invisible. Blocks now appear the frame they're painted, wearing the game's own mesh and `BlockMaterial` (`block_material` moved out of `block_spawn`, which `c0009`'s palette will want too).
[c0007] ## One bug the tests missed
[c0007] Running the game panicked on the main menu: a run condition is evaluated every frame whether or not the `in_state` beside it holds — Bevy runs them all rather than short-circuiting, so change detection in a condition can't miss a change. `resource_changed::<EditorLevel>` asked about a resource that doesn't exist until the editor is opened. Fixed with `resource_exists_and_changed` and pinned by a test that fails on the old condition.
[c0007] ## Verification
[c0007] 26 new tests, 106 green, `cargo build` clean at 19 warnings (unchanged). Also checked in the running game via a temporary driver system, since removed: the editor opens on `level0` with all 8 blocks dressed in the game mesh and material, and a mouse-driven paint through the real input path adds a ninth.
[c0007] One gap, recorded on the card: **not** visually confirmed. Bevy's own screenshot API returns solid black from this session, as `screencapture` does — so how it looks on screen rests on the material being the game's own rather than on a picture.
