[c0009] I've picked up c0009 and hit a fork that needs your call, so I'm parking here.
[c0009] **What I established first** (recorded in the card's Notes so it isn't redone):
[c0009] - Bevy 0.19's `Interaction` component is driven by `ui_focus_system`, which needs the whole UI stack — `UiPlugin`, layout, `UiStack`, visibility propagation, a camera with a `RenderTarget`. I spiked adding it to the editor's headless test app and it panics in two systems on a missing resource. So a click on a palette entry can't be tested the way `c0006`/`c0007` test a click on a cell: through the real window and the real pointer.
[c0009] - The palette will therefore hit-test itself against rectangles it computes — the same trade the editor already makes for the grid (`world_to_cell`, not mesh picking). One pure layout function gives every entry its rect; the spawner draws that rect and the click reads it, so what's on screen and what's clickable can't drift.
[c0009] **The question on the card**: the format reuses its letters across the three axes — `A` is Simple *and* SittingDuck *and* Start, `B`/`C` likewise, `D` on two. The token resolves that by position in the token; a keyboard has no positions. So "a shortcut matching its letter" can't be a bare letter for all three axes.
[c0009] I've put three schemes on the card — one modifier per axis, type-the-token, or bare letters with one axis winning each — and recommended the first, since it's the only one giving every entry a one-press shortcut without a mode. Answer on the card and I'll pick it back up.
