[c0011] **c0011 — Undo and redo** is in `review`, committed as `b917494`.
[c0011] ## What landed
[c0011] A new `src/editor/history.rs` holds the stack, the keys and the bar. An `Edit` is the two levels either side of it rather than a hand-written inverse — a `LevelDefinition` is a token grid plus ten small fields, so the pair is cheap, and it is the only form that reverses without an argument (the inverse of "take the top row away" has to carry the blocks that stood on it anyway).
[c0011] The three editing systems record through it. A drag is one entry because `c0007` already recorded the stroke as a whole; `finish_stroke` is now called by resize, settings and undo too, so anything the author does mid-drag ends that stroke rather than being swallowed by it.
[c0011] `Ctrl+Z` undoes, `Ctrl+Y` and `Ctrl+Shift+Z` redo, `Cmd` counts as `Ctrl`. The **History** bar sits under the settings panel, says what each step would take back ("painting 3 cells", "removing the bottom row", "changing Time limit"), and is hit-tested and kept off the play field exactly as that panel is.
[c0011] `EditorLevel::source` became the `Handle<LevelAsset>` instead of the path string — that is what an `AssetEvent::Modified` can be matched against, which is how a hand edit to the file underneath drops the history. `source_path()` is what `c0012` will save through.
[c0011] Two things fell out along the way: `c0008` left "warns first *or* is undoable" half-done, and it is now both; and a stroke left half-painted on the way out of the editor used to be dropped, making it the one edit that could not be taken back.
