[c0013] c0013 is in `review`.
[c0013] **What landed** — `F5` or a `Play` button starts a match on the level as it stands; `Escape` brings the editor back with every unsaved edit intact.
[c0013] - **One question, one place**: `Levels` gained `playtest: Option<Handle<LevelAsset>>` and `current_handle` prefers it. Arena, blocks, win criteria and the readiness check all go through `current_handle`, so one field redirects all of them — and `handles`/`current_level` are never written, which is the "no campaign progress disturbed" criterion by construction.
[c0013] - **The played level is a copy** added to `Assets` and dropped when the playtest ends, so nothing on the path reads the file.
[c0013] - **Win/lose forks**: a playtest goes home to `GameState::Editor` with nothing banked; a campaign match still goes to `PostMatch`. `PlayerState` is set either way, which is how the new fourth panel says "the last playtest was won / lost / back from".
[c0013] - **The editor clears the stage** on the way in (`playtest_teardown`), since the game's own teardown lives at `OnExit(PostMatch)` which a playtest never visits.
[c0013] - `close_on_esc` stands down during a playtest; each playtest deals a fresh three balls; `game_start` stops any stray playtest so the menu can't leave the campaign shadowed.
